WEBVTT

00:14.500 --> 00:17.570
[Xiacheng Pier]

00:15.300 --> 00:16.340
We're finally here.

00:16.340 --> 00:17.540
Yeah, I'm exhausted.

00:33.190 --> 00:42.930
[Xiacheng Pier]

00:45.250 --> 00:47.110
Do you want to go back to Xiacheng?

00:47.800 --> 00:49.120
What kind of question is that?
Of course I do.

00:49.120 --> 00:51.050
I don't want to go back to Xiacheng.

00:51.490 --> 00:53.950
I don't really have anything
tying me there.

00:55.560 --> 00:56.890
You can go back for me.

00:58.030 --> 01:02.050
♪ The setting sun sinks low into the sea ♪

00:58.950 --> 00:59.740
Shrimpie.

01:01.740 --> 01:03.740
Looks like you were wrong after all.

01:03.840 --> 01:05.160
We still came back together.

01:04.720 --> 01:07.130
♪ And the ship goes down into the flames ♪

01:08.110 --> 01:10.090
Zhang Haixia, don't worry.

01:08.270 --> 01:11.090
♪ You're standing by my side ♪

01:10.170 --> 01:11.220
Stick with me,

01:11.700 --> 01:14.170
and we'll make a name for ourselves
in Balongzhou.

01:14.170 --> 01:17.770
♪ Time is like a plague,
devouring yesterday ♪

01:14.700 --> 01:16.450
When the time comes,
we'll return to Xiacheng in glory

01:16.450 --> 01:17.850
and see Mentor together.

01:17.850 --> 01:19.010
Let's go, Shrimpie.

01:20.110 --> 01:22.730
♪ Yet I've searched through
every archive ♪

01:20.810 --> 01:21.730
Balongzhou,

01:23.110 --> 01:23.970
here we come!

01:24.350 --> 01:26.020
♪ Filled with endless lies ♪

01:28.420 --> 01:32.570
♪ The opening pages of this story
are woven from deceit ♪

01:33.090 --> 01:35.979
♪ A trial written into fate ♪

01:36.759 --> 01:42.810
♪ Through the mist I search your face—
are you still the same? ♪

01:44.229 --> 01:48.200
♪ The wind carries away the goodbye
we never said ♪

01:46.450 --> 01:49.720
[Inquiry Office]

01:49.090 --> 01:51.890
♪ The butterfly upon your shoulder ♪

01:50.460 --> 01:51.180
Plague!

01:52.550 --> 01:58.160
♪ Stayed with you to witness
this bustling world ♪

01:57.770 --> 01:59.229
You're heading to Jinfan?

01:59.250 --> 01:59.740
Yes.

02:00.780 --> 02:01.640
What about you?

02:02.180 --> 02:03.180
What's your plan?

02:05.260 --> 02:07.460
I'll take him back to the Archives first

02:07.580 --> 02:08.780
and look for Mentor.

02:09.180 --> 02:10.460
I wonder if Mentor still remembers

02:10.460 --> 02:11.390
what I look like.

02:13.040 --> 02:13.770
That's good.

02:15.190 --> 02:17.070
I won't be in need of this money anyway
now that I'm back.

02:17.070 --> 02:19.670
Switch to a bigger ship
for your trip to Jinfan.

02:20.140 --> 02:21.730
You know I won't take it.

02:21.890 --> 02:22.950
I have my own money.

02:23.470 --> 02:24.600
This is a principle.

02:27.140 --> 02:28.780
What needed repaying has been repaid,

02:28.780 --> 02:31.310
and what needed resenting
has been resented.

02:32.190 --> 02:33.160
Farewell.

02:45.520 --> 02:48.310
Give this money to Zhang Hailou.

02:50.770 --> 02:52.870
He's the Plague of Nanyang.

02:54.329 --> 02:54.940
It's him.

02:55.960 --> 02:56.500
Plague!

02:57.150 --> 02:57.750
Plague...

02:58.710 --> 02:59.430
Plague!

03:00.160 --> 03:01.190
Be careful.

03:03.380 --> 03:04.150
Plague!

03:04.420 --> 03:05.160
Plague!

04:32.150 --> 04:38.630
[Archives: The Nanyang Mystery]

04:38.890 --> 04:41.510
[Episode 11]

04:47.690 --> 04:48.510
Plague!

04:51.950 --> 04:52.500
Hello.

04:52.500 --> 04:54.159
Did you see someone coming out from here?

04:54.159 --> 04:54.770
Wearing a uniform,

04:54.770 --> 04:55.890
carrying someone on his back?

04:55.890 --> 04:57.470
No. Go check over there.

04:57.720 --> 04:58.320
Thank you.

04:59.700 --> 05:01.110
Hello, sir. Did you

05:01.150 --> 05:02.330
see someone

05:02.330 --> 05:03.330
coming out from here,

05:03.330 --> 05:04.360
wearing a uniform,

05:04.360 --> 05:06.220
and carrying someone on his back?

05:06.500 --> 05:07.100
No, I didn't.

05:07.100 --> 05:07.980
No, no, I didn't.

05:07.980 --> 05:08.690
Thank you.

05:12.690 --> 05:13.250
Sir.

05:13.800 --> 05:14.600
Hello, sir.

05:15.130 --> 05:16.120
Did you see

05:16.120 --> 05:17.680
a man in a uniform coming out from here,

05:17.680 --> 05:19.340
carrying someone on his back?

05:20.560 --> 05:21.720
I saw you on the ship.

05:21.810 --> 05:23.760
You were with that tall guy.

05:23.780 --> 05:25.050
You guys got separated, right?

05:25.050 --> 05:25.980
Yes, yes, that's right.

05:25.980 --> 05:26.770
He's my friend.

05:26.770 --> 05:28.600
Did you see which way he went?

05:30.270 --> 05:31.220
No, I didn't.

05:31.390 --> 05:32.180
But

05:33.159 --> 05:35.290
I'd like to borrow something from you.

05:35.830 --> 05:36.890
Borrow something?

05:37.580 --> 05:38.540
Money?

05:39.250 --> 05:40.740
I have no money.

05:40.930 --> 05:42.040
I'm in a hurry to find my friend.

05:42.040 --> 05:44.040
His friend left some money with me,

05:44.040 --> 05:45.500
so I need to bring it to him.

05:45.680 --> 05:46.540
It's not money.

05:46.870 --> 05:47.659
S-Sir.

05:47.920 --> 05:48.909
Pardon me.

05:48.940 --> 05:50.310
I'm still in a hurry to find my friend,

05:50.310 --> 05:51.880
and I have a ship to catch soon.

05:51.880 --> 05:53.060
If you don't know,

05:53.060 --> 05:54.000
I won't bother you further.

05:54.000 --> 05:54.600
Thank you.

05:54.930 --> 05:56.310
Since that's the case,

05:56.590 --> 05:58.990
I can help you give the money
to your friend.

05:59.480 --> 06:00.220
You?

06:00.920 --> 06:02.180
I don't even know you.

06:02.560 --> 06:03.510
What do you want?

06:04.360 --> 06:06.220
Since you're so worried,

06:06.240 --> 06:07.620
I can exchange my money

06:08.720 --> 06:09.690
with yours.

06:10.560 --> 06:11.240
However,

06:11.860 --> 06:13.980
I'd still like to borrow something
from you.

06:13.980 --> 06:15.910
What exactly do you want to borrow?

06:19.370 --> 06:20.040
Your face.

06:20.920 --> 06:22.280
What's your problem?

06:31.610 --> 06:36.330
[Xiacheng Pier]

06:48.830 --> 06:49.480
Hurry up.

06:49.870 --> 06:50.430
Move.

06:52.110 --> 06:52.880
Move, move.

06:57.740 --> 06:59.330
Master, Young Lady's back.

07:13.780 --> 07:14.770
Sweetie.

07:15.040 --> 07:23.980
[Xiacheng Pier]

07:15.560 --> 07:16.870
Dad, I'm back.

07:18.330 --> 07:21.620
Did you have a smooth trip, Sweetie?

07:22.860 --> 07:24.630
Thanks to Mr. Warner's escort,

07:25.040 --> 07:27.240
I was able to arrive safely in Xiacheng.

07:27.660 --> 07:29.870
Mr. Dong, I am Landon Warner.

07:30.120 --> 07:32.190
I'm Miss Dong's business partner.

07:32.250 --> 07:36.610
[Xiacheng Pier]

07:32.390 --> 07:33.630
It's a pleasure to meet you.

07:33.630 --> 07:34.430
I hope

07:34.690 --> 07:36.830
we'll have a pleasant cooperation
in our future business.

07:36.830 --> 07:37.720
I'm old now,

07:38.659 --> 07:41.260
and I washed my hands of foreign trade
long ago.

07:41.480 --> 07:43.210
Now I just run a few small trades

07:43.220 --> 07:46.420
and wait for my daughter
to take over the family business.

07:48.540 --> 07:49.310
I'm afraid,

07:50.040 --> 07:51.600
Mr. Warner, your business

07:51.980 --> 07:53.840
might not be easy for me to take on.

07:56.220 --> 07:58.000
Your daughter used my musketeers

07:58.000 --> 08:00.760
to round up so many pirates in Nan'an.

08:01.070 --> 08:02.220
As you Chinese say,

08:02.300 --> 08:04.010
"boldness stems from superb skill."

08:04.010 --> 08:07.540
She's really a worthy daughter
of Shichang, the shipping king.

08:08.010 --> 08:09.360
In those containers,

08:09.390 --> 08:10.000
there are many

08:10.000 --> 08:11.740
unidentified corpses.

08:12.250 --> 08:13.500
If the police ask about this,

08:13.500 --> 08:14.360
should I say

08:14.720 --> 08:16.430
they're related to the Dong family

08:16.430 --> 08:17.450
or not?

08:21.500 --> 08:22.500
It's all my fault.

08:23.000 --> 08:24.570
I've spent my whole life doing business

08:24.570 --> 08:26.750
and made many enemies along the way,

08:27.130 --> 08:29.660
and now I even got my daughter
dragged into it.

08:30.220 --> 08:31.010
However,

08:31.790 --> 08:33.770
this is my hometown.

08:35.289 --> 08:36.049
If anyone

08:37.200 --> 08:40.789
dares to scheme against or threaten me
here,

08:41.120 --> 08:41.980
I'll make sure

08:42.549 --> 08:44.860
they don't leave Xiacheng alive.

08:51.910 --> 08:53.200
You must be exhausted from the journey.

08:53.200 --> 08:55.140
Mr. Warner, please get in the car.

08:55.160 --> 08:56.560
Let's head back and rest.

08:57.150 --> 08:57.740
Please.

09:06.170 --> 09:07.600
Please take the car behind.

09:07.600 --> 09:10.860
Our Master and Young Lady
still have some catching up to do.

09:11.700 --> 09:14.580
[Xiacheng Pier]

09:13.740 --> 09:15.610
Get ready to leave, boys!

09:17.960 --> 09:20.000
Aren't we supposed to take the initiation?

09:20.000 --> 09:22.290
So? We're still doing business with them?

09:22.290 --> 09:23.460
Yes, of course.

09:23.670 --> 09:24.390
I don't believe

09:24.390 --> 09:26.320
Victory will always be on her side.

09:45.890 --> 09:47.150
Finally back.

09:48.480 --> 09:51.380
Why did you suddenly
return to Xiacheng this time

09:51.970 --> 09:53.940
with so many foreigners?

09:54.030 --> 09:55.290
Did something happen?

09:57.390 --> 09:58.850
Have you made any progress

09:59.250 --> 10:01.180
on what I asked you to investigate?

10:02.870 --> 10:04.770
All the information you requested is here.

10:04.520 --> 10:10.040
[Map of Xiacheng City]

10:04.890 --> 10:06.220
I've had someone decrypt

10:06.220 --> 10:07.740
the telegram you sent me

10:08.490 --> 10:10.230
from the Nan'an.

10:10.720 --> 10:13.210
It was encrypted

10:13.240 --> 10:14.980
with a military encryption method.

10:14.980 --> 10:16.190
This telegram

10:16.270 --> 10:18.720
was sent to a warlord force,

10:19.000 --> 10:19.500
but

10:20.500 --> 10:22.100
that unit is rather unusual.

10:22.200 --> 10:24.050
You truly are a man of the military.

10:24.050 --> 10:25.180
Unusual in what way?

10:25.390 --> 10:26.510
They keep

10:26.960 --> 10:28.420
an extremely low profile.

10:28.820 --> 10:31.950
The information that can be discovered
is very limited.

10:32.790 --> 10:35.650
They were last seen around Beilian,

10:35.670 --> 10:38.820
led by a man named Mo Yungao.

10:39.890 --> 10:41.620
We're only sure of his name,

10:42.340 --> 10:45.000
but there isn't even
a single clear photo of him.

10:47.150 --> 10:50.110
The final part of
this decrypted telegram says,

10:50.340 --> 10:52.930
"Members of the Southern Archives
have been eliminated.

10:50.970 --> 10:53.020
[Telegram Draft]

10:53.080 --> 10:55.030
All bodies have been recovered.

10:55.220 --> 10:57.320
Will meet in Xiacheng as agreed.

10:57.890 --> 10:59.750
This telegram serves as notice."

11:08.300 --> 11:09.880
Mo Yungao?

11:10.480 --> 11:12.880
So you're the one
messing with my Archives.

11:18.170 --> 11:21.180
It seems a bloodbath
is coming to Xiacheng.

11:38.930 --> 11:40.590
This street is still the same.

11:45.330 --> 11:46.200
Zhang Hailou.

11:46.410 --> 11:47.470
If you keep crying,

11:47.520 --> 11:48.860
I won't carry you anymore.

11:48.860 --> 11:52.040
Zhang Haixia, walk faster, okay?

11:52.060 --> 11:52.670
Okay.

11:53.460 --> 11:54.290
Zhang Hailou,

11:54.320 --> 11:55.500
watch your mouth!

11:55.860 --> 11:57.320
As if I owed you something.

11:57.540 --> 11:58.470
Seriously.

11:58.520 --> 12:00.450
I don't believe I can't handle you!

12:01.120 --> 12:02.200
I was wrong!

12:10.220 --> 12:14.210
[A Hundred Flowers in Bloom]

12:10.790 --> 12:11.430
Shrimpie.

12:12.600 --> 12:13.460
We've arrived.

12:22.320 --> 12:22.890
Sir,

12:22.960 --> 12:24.140
what do you need?

12:27.390 --> 12:28.100
Who are you?

12:28.340 --> 12:29.600
Why are you in my house?

12:30.010 --> 12:32.760
I sell dried seafood.

12:33.350 --> 12:35.290
Did you come to the wrong place?

12:43.660 --> 12:45.520
What about the previous tenants?

12:45.800 --> 12:46.560
I've been

12:46.630 --> 12:48.260
running this shop for years.

12:48.610 --> 12:49.930
No one has lived here.

12:51.830 --> 12:52.970
I used to live here.

12:54.500 --> 12:55.900
But it was a long time ago.

12:57.180 --> 12:59.470
Maybe your family moved away.

13:02.080 --> 13:05.640
[Yuanbao Clinic]

13:03.390 --> 13:05.000
Moving away without even
leaving a message—

13:05.000 --> 13:06.460
that's typical of Mentor.

13:07.070 --> 13:07.740
Shrimpie,

13:08.360 --> 13:09.370
let's go to the Archives.

13:08.720 --> 13:10.290
[Yuanbao Clinic]

13:10.420 --> 13:21.650
[Danan Telegraph Office]

13:11.080 --> 13:12.940
I throw more accurately than you.

13:14.650 --> 13:16.070
You throw terribly!

13:28.980 --> 13:30.580
Zhang Hailou, Zhang Haixia!

13:30.600 --> 13:31.460
Mentor's here.

13:31.530 --> 13:32.360
Come here.

13:34.850 --> 13:35.870
Mentor.

13:35.890 --> 13:38.110
Why does the front of the Archives

13:38.200 --> 13:39.790
say "Telegraph Office"?

13:43.550 --> 13:45.620
Because the Archives
is a secret organization

13:45.620 --> 13:47.270
directly under
the Maritime Supervisory Office.

13:47.270 --> 13:48.870
We must not let ordinary people
know about it,

13:48.870 --> 13:50.270
so it has to be disguised.

13:50.620 --> 13:51.220
Mentor!

13:51.790 --> 13:52.790
Did you hear that?

13:52.790 --> 13:53.840
This is a secret.

13:53.960 --> 13:56.490
To the public, we are
Danan Telegraph Office.

13:57.100 --> 13:58.240
But Mentor,

13:58.400 --> 14:01.060
will this really keep us
from being discovered?

14:02.380 --> 14:05.230
Within an organization
vast and complex enough,

14:05.460 --> 14:07.720
there are always redundant departments.

14:07.720 --> 14:09.150
As long as we hide in such places,

14:09.150 --> 14:10.480
we stay under the radar.

14:10.960 --> 14:12.320
Just like hermit crabs.

14:15.950 --> 14:16.670
Mentor,

14:16.690 --> 14:19.060
when can I go play in the Archives?

14:19.800 --> 14:21.250
Focus on learning the ropes first.

14:21.250 --> 14:23.150
Once you become a full employee,
you'll be allowed into the Archives.

14:23.150 --> 14:24.050
Let's go home.

14:28.220 --> 14:31.990
[Danan Telegraph Office]

14:29.900 --> 14:30.700
Zhang Hailou.

14:35.080 --> 14:35.770
Stop there!

14:35.820 --> 14:36.720
Come catch me!

14:37.700 --> 14:38.910
This is really nice.

14:37.760 --> 14:45.510
[Haili Bank]

14:39.240 --> 14:39.860
Let me see.

14:39.860 --> 14:40.630
If you don't like it,
there's also this one.

14:40.630 --> 14:41.290
Never mind.

14:41.370 --> 14:42.000
Just take a look.

14:42.000 --> 14:43.470
These are all good stuff.

14:51.380 --> 14:53.530
[Haili Bank]

14:54.290 --> 14:55.390
Are these all registered?

14:55.390 --> 14:56.390
Yes, don't worry.

14:56.390 --> 14:57.320
You can just come directly.

14:57.320 --> 14:57.650
Okay.

14:57.820 --> 14:59.200
I'll come to you again next time.

14:59.200 --> 15:00.200
He will receive you.

15:00.200 --> 15:02.200
You can also talk to me in the future.

15:03.770 --> 15:04.650
Hello, ma'am.

15:04.790 --> 15:06.270
You need to register here.

15:06.580 --> 15:07.240
Here, right?

15:07.240 --> 15:07.740
Yes.

15:07.750 --> 15:08.200
Okay.

15:09.840 --> 15:10.360
Sir.

15:11.430 --> 15:13.060
Sir, how can I help you?

15:14.760 --> 15:16.410
Wasn't this place
the Danan Telegraph Office before?

15:16.410 --> 15:17.690
How did it become a bank?

15:17.690 --> 15:19.040
Sir, this place has always been a bank.

15:19.040 --> 15:20.790
I've never heard of a telegraph office.

15:20.790 --> 15:22.220
Did you get the wrong place?

15:22.220 --> 15:22.750
That's impossible.

15:22.750 --> 15:24.390
I worked here for many years.

15:25.440 --> 15:27.360
I couldn't have remembered it wrong.

15:27.360 --> 15:29.220
How many years have you been open?

15:29.290 --> 15:30.620
It's been quite a few years.

15:30.620 --> 15:32.430
But as for what it was before we opened,

15:32.430 --> 15:33.290
I'm not so sure.

15:33.510 --> 15:34.400
I'm sorry, sir.

15:34.630 --> 15:36.960
Is there anything else
I can help you with?

15:47.740 --> 15:49.890
[Maritime Supervisory Office]

15:50.030 --> 15:52.650
This is
the Nanyang Maritime Supervisory Office.

15:52.650 --> 15:54.450
Okay, I'll check for you in a bit.

16:01.410 --> 16:01.960
Hello.

16:04.020 --> 16:05.640
Excuse me, do you know

16:06.270 --> 16:08.400
where the Southern Archives moved to?

16:08.420 --> 16:10.230
The Southern Archives?

16:11.510 --> 16:12.640
Have you heard of it?

16:12.770 --> 16:13.770
Never heard of it.

16:13.820 --> 16:14.760
What Archives?

16:15.080 --> 16:17.880
This is
the Nanyang Maritime Supervisory Office.

16:21.250 --> 16:22.250
Here's the thing.

16:22.770 --> 16:24.370
The Southern Archives is

16:24.520 --> 16:27.100
an agency under
the Nanyang Maritime Supervisory Office.

16:27.100 --> 16:28.410
Since it's a...

16:31.020 --> 16:33.250
Since it's
a secret investigation organization,

16:33.250 --> 16:34.790
it has always used

16:34.810 --> 16:37.340
the name "Danan Telegraph Office"
as a cover.

16:37.340 --> 16:39.010
Actually, broadly speaking,

16:39.550 --> 16:40.600
we can be considered colleagues.

16:40.600 --> 16:41.600
Now that I have returned to the country,

16:41.600 --> 16:42.840
I found that
the Southern Archives has moved,

16:42.840 --> 16:44.550
but I don't know where it moved to.

16:44.550 --> 16:46.210
Could you please check for me?

16:47.840 --> 16:49.030
Please wait a moment.

16:49.030 --> 16:49.480
Okay.

17:17.910 --> 17:18.569
Sir,

17:18.619 --> 17:19.430
I've asked around.

17:19.430 --> 17:21.960
There is no such "Archives"
as you mentioned.

17:22.109 --> 17:23.310
How is that possible?

17:24.050 --> 17:25.290
The name is "the Southern Archives."

17:25.290 --> 17:26.460
You must have gotten it wrong.

17:26.460 --> 17:27.680
I just asked some senior commissioners

17:27.680 --> 17:29.810
who have worked here for over 20 years,

17:29.920 --> 17:30.850
and they said that in all these years

17:30.850 --> 17:33.330
since Nanyang Maritime Supervisory Office
was established,

17:33.330 --> 17:35.690
there has never been an agency called

17:35.720 --> 17:37.180
"the Southern Archives."

17:37.310 --> 17:38.420
Are you mistaken?

17:42.850 --> 17:44.210
It must be you who are mistaken.

17:44.210 --> 17:48.810
[Inquiry Desk]

17:46.110 --> 17:47.460
Please keep an eye on my brother for me.

17:47.460 --> 17:48.520
I'll go ask myself.

17:49.010 --> 17:49.500
Sir!

17:51.730 --> 17:52.590
What do you mean

17:52.590 --> 17:54.420
the Southern Archives never existed?

17:54.420 --> 17:56.290
Look, if it doesn't exist,
it doesn't exist.

17:56.290 --> 17:58.620
We've never heard of any Archives either.

17:58.940 --> 17:59.570
Young man,

17:59.830 --> 18:00.380
look,

18:00.910 --> 18:02.190
this is our file.

18:02.050 --> 18:04.520
[Files of
the Nanyang Maritime Supervisory Office]

18:05.270 --> 18:06.670
Absolutely impossible.

18:07.250 --> 18:08.350
I was trained and employed
at the Southern Archives

18:08.350 --> 18:10.150
for over 10 years.

18:09.780 --> 18:12.110
[Registry of Affiliated Agencies
Reporting to the Maritime Supervisory Office]

18:10.500 --> 18:12.230
I've always been an agent here,

18:12.250 --> 18:14.410
and I even worked in the office of
the Archives.

18:14.410 --> 18:15.640
I've handled countless mysterious cases.

18:15.640 --> 18:17.380
Every file should be on record.

18:15.690 --> 18:16.300
[Registry of Affiliated Agencies
Reporting to the Maritime Supervisory Office]

18:18.350 --> 18:18.810
Look.

18:19.750 --> 18:20.790
This is my badge.

18:22.750 --> 18:23.830
[Zhang Hailou]

18:23.160 --> 18:25.170
We've never issued any badge like this.

18:25.170 --> 18:25.990
Besides,

18:26.170 --> 18:27.710
we manage ship crews here.

18:28.070 --> 18:30.400
Investigations are none of our business.

18:36.330 --> 18:36.850
Let go!

18:38.460 --> 18:39.120
Say it!

18:40.000 --> 18:41.800
Where is the Southern Archives?

18:41.980 --> 18:42.610
Speak!

18:43.810 --> 18:45.740
I really don't know anything about

18:46.190 --> 18:48.210
the Southern Archives.

18:49.750 --> 18:51.070
You are lying!

18:52.520 --> 18:53.890
I'm not lying...

18:54.260 --> 18:56.060
I'm telling the truth...

18:58.050 --> 19:00.110
I'm telling the truth...

19:05.800 --> 19:06.930
If you're not lying,

19:11.060 --> 19:13.290
then the Southern Archives doesn't exist.

19:13.290 --> 19:14.490
How is that possible?

19:22.770 --> 19:25.030
If the Southern Archives doesn't exist,

19:27.510 --> 19:30.240
then what do the past decades
of my life amount to?

19:30.590 --> 19:32.470
Commissioner , what happened?

19:34.190 --> 19:35.910
Why would Mentor lie to me?

19:45.860 --> 19:51.460
[Maritime Supervisory Office]

19:49.150 --> 19:50.260
Leave immediately. Move.

19:50.260 --> 19:52.460
There's no one here you are looking for.

19:54.860 --> 19:56.050
Shrimpie. Careful.

20:01.980 --> 20:03.230
[Archives Room]

20:03.920 --> 20:04.550
Speak!

20:04.570 --> 20:05.160
Let go!

20:07.570 --> 20:08.830
You're lying!

20:09.070 --> 20:13.960
[Maritime Supervisory Office]

20:11.400 --> 20:14.260
Come check this out,
fresh roasted sweet potatoes!

20:14.290 --> 20:16.740
Soft and sweet roasted sweet potatoes!

20:18.310 --> 20:20.380
Freshly roasted sweet potatoes!

20:21.160 --> 20:24.180
Soft and sweet roasted sweet potatoes!

20:27.400 --> 20:29.720
Please keep an eye on my brother for me
for a bit.

20:29.720 --> 20:30.430
Okay, okay.

20:33.790 --> 20:37.080
[Archives Room]

21:02.380 --> 21:02.680
[Files]

22:06.570 --> 22:08.330
Mom, what are we having today?

22:08.900 --> 22:10.140
We're having stir-fried shrimp today.

22:10.140 --> 22:11.140
Let's hurry home!

22:12.680 --> 22:13.680
Okay. Let's go.

22:13.700 --> 22:14.700
Let's hurry home!

22:16.330 --> 22:17.500
Let's go!

22:27.520 --> 22:31.050
[Dehexing]

23:05.110 --> 23:07.040
I finally brought you home, but now

23:08.910 --> 23:10.710
the home's gone, the job's gone,

23:10.960 --> 23:13.020
and the Archives doesn't even exist.

23:14.270 --> 23:15.270
Do you believe it?

23:23.840 --> 23:24.940
Well, I sure don't.

23:26.660 --> 23:28.250
According to the newspapers,

23:28.250 --> 23:29.560
the Chen warlords

23:30.750 --> 23:33.010
have gained complete control of Xiacheng.

23:33.010 --> 23:34.660
We've sent 36

23:34.660 --> 23:35.890
regular monthly report telegrams,

23:35.890 --> 23:37.350
but there's been no reply.

23:37.350 --> 23:38.480
The last one was sent

23:39.090 --> 23:41.090
after we came back from Panhua Reef.

23:41.460 --> 23:43.000
Maybe something happened to the Archives,

23:43.000 --> 23:43.940
or someone

23:43.940 --> 23:45.220
erased its existence.

23:47.400 --> 23:48.160
Even if it was erased,

23:48.160 --> 23:50.090
how could it be done so thoroughly?

23:50.570 --> 23:54.030
Could this be the work of
whoever's spreading that toxic weed?

24:06.000 --> 24:09.410
[Chocolate]

24:15.330 --> 24:16.470
Times are hard.

24:16.510 --> 24:17.640
We won't meet again.

24:18.190 --> 24:19.660
If your obsession persists

24:19.660 --> 24:21.260
and you are still perplexed,

24:21.680 --> 24:23.210
you may come here for a chat.

24:23.810 --> 24:24.410
Remember,

24:24.750 --> 24:25.920
it's best we don't meet.

24:25.920 --> 24:27.720
Nothing needs to be said anyway.

24:29.720 --> 24:31.380
This woman is so resourceful.

24:32.510 --> 24:34.240
Maybe I should ask her for help.

24:42.390 --> 24:43.720
The Southern Archives?

24:52.870 --> 24:54.280
Sir, this way please.

24:56.990 --> 24:58.420
My Lady, he's here.

25:14.410 --> 25:15.720
I thought you'd wander out there

25:15.720 --> 25:16.590
for a few weeks

25:16.590 --> 25:17.720
before coming to me.

25:18.080 --> 25:20.010
I didn't expect you to come so soon.

25:21.250 --> 25:22.580
Are your wounds healed?

25:23.810 --> 25:25.670
All the doctors on your ship died.

25:26.500 --> 25:27.740
I treated my wounds myself.

25:27.740 --> 25:29.940
I don't think they could heal very well.

25:39.750 --> 25:41.350
Miss Dong, I have a question.

25:43.790 --> 25:45.120
When we were on the ship,

25:46.400 --> 25:47.810
you refused to talk to me.

25:48.720 --> 25:50.450
But after getting off the ship,

25:51.030 --> 25:52.690
you wrote me that invitation.

25:54.510 --> 25:55.550
Hermit crabs.

25:57.810 --> 25:59.140
The Southern Archives.

26:01.050 --> 26:02.310
Do you know something?

26:04.460 --> 26:06.460
I've never heard of any "Archives."

26:07.050 --> 26:08.590
Did you have a dream or something?

26:08.590 --> 26:10.030
The former Danan Telegraph Office

26:10.030 --> 26:11.290
was the Southern Archives.

26:11.290 --> 26:13.310
My mentor, Zhang Haiqi,

26:14.240 --> 26:15.500
was the Director of it.

26:15.660 --> 26:16.590
Where is she now?

26:16.640 --> 26:19.100
And where did the Southern Archives
move to?

26:19.470 --> 26:21.730
I have no idea what you're talking about.

26:26.740 --> 26:27.420
Miss Dong.

26:28.940 --> 26:30.600
You kept me alive on that ship.

26:31.680 --> 26:33.610
If you need me to get anything done,

26:34.480 --> 26:35.750
you can just tell me.

26:37.140 --> 26:38.940
But right now, I just need to know

26:41.350 --> 26:44.810
that the existence of
the Southern Archives meant something,

26:44.850 --> 26:46.850
so my friend didn't die for nothing.

26:48.740 --> 26:50.010
Even if it's gone now,

26:50.660 --> 26:52.920
I could accept it
as a cruel twist of fate.

26:53.590 --> 26:56.320
My only fear is that
after everything we've done,

26:56.480 --> 26:58.740
it turns out to be nothing but a daydream,

27:01.160 --> 27:02.820
and no one will even remember.

27:13.230 --> 27:14.760
Let me tell you a story then.

27:15.500 --> 27:17.700
Once upon a time, there were two agents.

27:19.200 --> 27:20.500
One was smart,

27:22.180 --> 27:22.910
and the other

27:23.610 --> 27:24.850
was a troublemaker.

27:26.270 --> 27:27.930
The two of them were partners,

27:28.440 --> 27:30.370
investigating cases everywhere.

27:30.440 --> 27:32.300
They solved many cases together.

27:33.250 --> 27:34.610
But the troublemaker

27:35.200 --> 27:36.800
was always causing trouble,

27:37.050 --> 27:38.280
and the smart one

27:38.900 --> 27:41.030
had to constantly clean up his messes.

27:41.510 --> 27:43.110
Many years passed like this.

27:43.660 --> 27:45.830
During a case on a reef,

27:46.790 --> 27:47.940
the two agents

27:48.400 --> 27:50.600
went deep into the enemy's stronghold.

27:51.200 --> 27:52.600
There were many enemies,

27:53.270 --> 27:55.300
and there were only 2 of them.

27:58.130 --> 28:01.810
They should have retreated right after
they finished searching for evidence,

28:01.810 --> 28:03.160
but the troublemaker

28:03.180 --> 28:04.530
acted on his own.

28:04.990 --> 28:06.740
To get more information,

28:07.030 --> 28:09.040
he did something very risky.

28:10.090 --> 28:12.750
He actually revealed his identity
to the enemy,

28:12.920 --> 28:15.310
leaking the Archives' information
to the enemy.

28:15.310 --> 28:17.570
Have you heard of a man
named Salty Zhang?

28:17.750 --> 28:18.810
This guy belongs to

28:19.330 --> 28:22.920
the Southern Archives under
the Nanyang Maritime Supervisory Office.

28:22.920 --> 28:24.110
Yet it was precisely

28:24.110 --> 28:25.910
this small, unnecessary action

28:26.680 --> 28:28.940
that ultimately led to a great disaster.

28:29.330 --> 28:31.190
Because he exposed his identity,

28:31.330 --> 28:32.090
the enemy quickly found

28:32.090 --> 28:34.330
the headquarters of the Archives.

28:34.490 --> 28:35.750
The enemy moved so fast

28:35.960 --> 28:37.590
that the headquarters
was caught off guard.

28:37.590 --> 28:38.770
Overnight,

28:39.090 --> 28:41.790
all the agents at the headquarters
were slaughtered,

28:41.790 --> 28:43.660
and the agents scattered everywhere

28:43.660 --> 28:46.390
were also continuously hunted down
by the enemy—

28:46.990 --> 28:48.790
until they found these 2 agents.

28:50.330 --> 28:52.130
The troublemaker survived,

28:53.090 --> 28:54.070
but the smart one

28:55.470 --> 28:56.470
failed to escape.

29:00.870 --> 29:01.980
Are you finished?

29:02.560 --> 29:03.570
Why so impatient?

29:03.870 --> 29:06.400
I haven't got to the best part
of the story yet.

29:07.030 --> 29:08.180
The story goes

29:09.170 --> 29:10.860
that the smart agent,

29:11.230 --> 29:13.950
in the closing report of the reef case,

29:14.530 --> 29:16.130
wrote a paragraph like this.

29:18.400 --> 29:19.730
It's on your right side.

29:21.440 --> 29:23.040
Would you like to have a read?

29:43.510 --> 29:47.070
[Major Oversight]
[Conclusions and Warnings]

29:43.880 --> 29:45.240
The Panhua Reef Case

29:45.610 --> 29:46.700
is still pending,

29:47.330 --> 29:48.390
full of mysteries.

29:49.050 --> 29:50.310
During the operation,

29:50.530 --> 29:53.240
the agents' identities
and the Archives' information were leaked,

29:53.240 --> 29:54.510
which could cause future trouble.

29:54.510 --> 29:55.840
I hope Director is aware

29:55.850 --> 29:56.980
so that countermeasures can be prepared.

29:56.130 --> 29:58.730
[Case Closure Report]

29:58.810 --> 30:00.310
[Major Oversight]
[Conclusions and Warnings]

29:59.140 --> 30:01.000
As for the oversight in this case,

30:01.570 --> 30:03.900
I'm willing to bear full responsibility.

30:23.330 --> 30:23.900
Alright.

30:25.370 --> 30:26.830
That's the end of my story.

30:27.630 --> 30:28.780
You may leave now.

30:38.950 --> 30:40.000
Who exactly are you?
